TREE(1)                       User Commands

NAME
    tree - display a directory tree

SYNOPSIS
    tree [-a] [-d] [-L depth] [directory...]

DESCRIPTION
    Prints a sorted ASCII directory tree, followed by directory and file
    counts. -a includes hidden names, -d lists only directories and -L
    limits depth (1 shows direct children). The default path is . and the
    default depth limit is 64. Directory names are coloured on terminals.
    A symbolic link is shown as "name -> target", counted as a file and
    not entered.

SEE ALSO
    sh(1), man(1), index(7)
